  "definition": "Educational Requirements for Social Work Associate",
  "effectiveDate": "2026-08-24",
  "expirationDate": "2036-08-24",
  "historyNote": "#13903, eff 5-14-24; ss by #14641, eff 8-24-26, EXPIRES: 8-24-36",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Mhp 308.01",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mhp300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Mhp 308.01 Educational Requirements for Social Work Associate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mhp 308.01 Educational Requirements for Social Work Associate. Applicants shall meet one of the following requirements to be eligible for licensure as a social work associate:\n\n(a) If graduated with a bachelor’s degree in clinical mental health, social work, psychology, behavioral health counseling, human services discipline, or equivalent program from an accredited college or university:\n\n(1) Have completed 300 hours of social work or mental health education within the degree-granting program or separately;\n\n(2) Have completed 300 hours of supervised practical training within the degree granting program or separately;\n\n(3) Have completed 4,000 hours of supervised work experience in no less than 2 years but no more than 4 years;\n\n(4) Have passed the national ASWB associate level examination; and\n\n(5) During the period of supervised practice, have completed 30 hours of continuing education, in addition to what is described in (a)(1) in all of the following:\n\na. Ethical and professional behavior;\n\nb. Advancing human rights and social, racial, economic, and environmental justice;\n\nc. Anti-racism, diversity, equity, and inclusion in practice;\n\nd. Practice-informed research and research-informed practice;\n\ne. Policy practice;\n\nf. Engagement with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities;\n\ng. Assessing individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities;\n\nh. Intervention with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities; and\n\ni. Evaluation of practice with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities; or\n\n(b) If graduated with an associate’s degree in clinical mental health, social work, psychology, behavioral health counseling, human services discipline, or equivalent program from an accredited college or university:\n\n(1) Have completed 300 hours of social work or mental health education within the degree-granting program or separately;\n\n(2) Have completed 300 hours of supervised practical training within the degree granting program as part of the supervised work experience or separately;\n\n(3) Have completed 6,000 hours of supervised work experience in no fewer than 3 years;\n\n(4) Have passed the national ASWB associate level examination; and\n\n(5) During the period of supervised practice, have completed 30 hours of continuing education in addition to what is described in (b)(1) in all of the following:\n\na. Ethical and professional behavior;\n\nb. Advancing human rights and social, racial, economic, and environmental justice;\n\nc. Anti-racism, diversity, equity, and inclusion in practice;\n\nd. Practice-informed research and research-informed practice;\n\ne. Policy practice;\n\nf. Engagement with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities;\n\ng. Assessing individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities;\n\nh. Intervention with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities; and\n\ni. Evaluation of practice with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities.\n\nSource. #13903, eff 5-14-24; ss by #14641, eff 8-24-26, EXPIRES: 8-24-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mhp300.html"
}
